  "worked_solution": "The notation $x\\to -{2}^{-}$ means that $x$ approaches $-2$ *from the left*.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227291/assets/ef61a0d8a90ec9d0b120b0b9bf47077c7c77887f457182c09ee36b7d78b8cf9f.png)\n\nFrom the given graph, we see that as $x$ approaches $-2$ from the left, the values of $f(x)$ increase, approaching $\\infty .$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -{2}^{-}$",
